# PROBE-ONLY: needs a probe build with a test-only BumperControl stub (not part of the tree; run_p_core.py --probe):
# ControlCollision -> AwardJackpot(2.0), ControlBallCaptured -> AwardJackpot(-1.5). On a normal build a_bump1 is the real
# BumperControl and the script fails. Positive-time AwardJackpot is checked through a real caller by pd_ldugg_m4.uh
# (sound id 57 and the glyph text at 340, mode-4 LDUGG bank completion, pirates_drop_banks.cpp:186). The negative-time
# (silent) branch has no real caller (every AwardJackpot call passes 0.0f, or ActivateRandomMagnet's positive return,
# pirates_drop_banks.cpp:234), so it is checked by this probe only.
# AwardJackpot (FT 0x424700, listing 1285-1309). Positive time: sound tabb85, glyph text at t + 2.0, SpecialAddScore
# adds the jackpot (1,000,000 after NewGame) to the score, the jackpot itself is not reset. Negative time: no sound, text time 1.5 + 2.0.
init window 960 666
init fixed_dt 10
init seed 1
10 key down new_game
11 key up new_game
200 dump before_a
220 event a_bump1 ControlCollision
230 dump after_a
230 expect jackpot == 1000000
230 expect n_score == 1000000 delta 219
220-230 expect text info_text_box display
220-230 expect sound 57   # tabb85wave (sounds.jsonl info AwardJackpot)
300 dump before_b
320 event a_bump1 ControlBallCaptured
330 dump after_b
330 expect jackpot == 1000000
330 expect n_score == 1000000 delta 319
320-330 expect text info_text_box display
320-330 expect none sound 57   # tabb85 id (sounds.jsonl info AwardJackpot, run 1); ball sounds (id 0) keep playing
400 quit
